[h1]LiveWire Extended - Whole Buildings, Outdoor Power and Breaker Boards[/h1]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer (server-authoritative) · Requires LiveWire[/b]

An optional add-on for [b]LiveWire[/b]. The inverter powers the appliances in a circle around it; LiveWire Extended carries that power further, without touching the game's generator settings. Remove it at any time (with breaker boards, an admin first switches every breaker back on from a board's menu): LiveWire goes back to its circle, with no leftover power.

[h2]Connect a whole building[/h2]

Right-click an inverter > LiveWire Extended > [b]Connect the building[/b] (Electrical 3). Every floor, the basement and a strip around the ground floor get power, even beyond the inverter's circle. Appliances are billed by the inverter as usual: consumption, breaker and battery still apply. One inverter per building.

[h2]Outdoor power terminal[/h2]

Craft a [b]power terminal[/b] (Electrical 3) or find one with electricians' gear. Place it anywhere, link it to an inverter with electric wire (same cable rules as LiveWire), then [b]draw its zone[/b] on the ground: up to 16 x 16 squares, rounded to the 8 x 8 blocks the game really powers. Perfect for a vegetable garden, a workshop or a house you built. Placed against a distant building, a linked terminal can connect that building too.

[h2]Breaker boards[/h2]

Hang a [b]breaker board[/b] (8, 16 or 24 modules) on a wall, link it to an inverter, install [b]15, 20 or 30 A breakers[/b] (found or crafted) and [b]wire each appliance[/b] to its breaker. Once a board serves a building, unwired appliances have no current. Breakers trip on their own when overloaded; label them with a pen, see the load in W and A and the energy of each circuit, [b]Locate[/b] what a breaker feeds. A [b]twilight switch[/b] keeps a circuit on from dusk to dawn. Some houses of the map already have a prewired, unlabelled board: find out which breaker feeds what. Works with My Tailor Is Rich's sewing machine and Functional Appliances 2.

[h2]See it[/h2]

"Show range" on the inverter outlines every extra powered block; the inverter screen lists the connected buildings and terminals. Translated in 10 languages.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

Needs LiveWire. Not compatible with LG Extended Electricity, which changes the generator range LiveWire relies on, nor with Knox Power (its own breaker system in houses). Outdoor squares follow the game's "generator outdoors" option.

[h2]Credits[/h2]

Created by batmanfr. Original code and models; no content taken from other mods.
